- system_vocabulary
- grove_role_runtime
- net
- pass

' One tree, many writers. A composition is a tree no single world holds: a
' table says, for each position in it, who writes there and who reads. Each
' world keeps what it writes at a root of its own (its side) and names
' each record, at its case, in the roots of that record's readers, where
' the kernel's pairwise publication carries it. No record is made twice. These are the rules that read the table,
' pure. Nothing here signs, and nothing here knows what a course or an
' order is.
'
' Who a position's writer is today is read off a seat: a record the maker
' writes, whose slot world names the world that fills it. A record is taken
' only from the world that writes its position, so a world that does not
' fill the seat is never read for it, whatever it publishes. That is the
' whole of who is believed.
'
' Nothing is requested and nothing is accepted. What a world can do is the
' empty places it writes. A row may name an action (apply): a record
' there is the action's arguments, its writer is whoever may ask, and the
' thing the position sits beneath is what is asked of. Whoever writes that
' thing applies the action, with the code its own world holds, and writes
' an answer beside the ask. No code crosses between worlds.
'
' What a world was given stays its own to show. A record written for it
' is held under its writer's signature, and so are the maker's table and
' seats. Together they are a proof that a world holding nothing of the
' composition checks against the maker's name, and asks nobody.
'
' A row may say what a record there must show (shows): the place of a
' record that names another composition and a position in it. A record at
' such a place stands only when it carries a proof of a record there that
' was written for the world that shows it, so what sits beneath it opens
' only then. Showing is the world's own choice: it fills the place, and
' its foot adds the proof from what the world holds.
+ weave
  + seg
    ' One segment of a position's path: a fixed name, or a capture that a
    ' path binds (the s of seats/[s]).
    : fixed=bool name=iota
  + who
    ' Who writes or reads a position: the maker, the world that keeps the
    ' composition; or whoever fills the seats at a path. A capture of that
    ' path that the position's own path binds picks one seat: under the
    ' same name, seats/[s] read from work/[s] is the seat that wrote the
    ' work. A capture under a name the position does not bind is left open,
    ' and means every seat there.
    : maker=bool seats=row[weave/seg]
  + position
    ' One row of the table. apply, where a row has one, names an action by
    ' its path beneath a world (/gov/course/extend). shows, where a row
    ' has one, names the place of the record that says what a record here
    ' must show (weave/want). stencil, where a row has one, names the
    ' declaration that states it the same way; a world that holds it holds
    ' the shape of a record here, and judges what it reads by it.
    : path=row[weave/seg] writer=weave/who readers=row[weave/who] apply=str shows=str stencil=str
  + comp
    ' A composition: the world that keeps it, where its tree sits in that
    ' world after the world's own name, and its table.
    : maker=nat rel=path table=row[weave/position]
  + side
    ' Where one world keeps what it writes of a composition.
    : me=nat root=path
  + bind
    : name=iota value=iota
  + tenure
    ' A world that has filled a seat, and this world's own epoch at which
    ' it held that the seat was no longer that world's: 0 while it is.
    : world=nat until=nat
  + spot
    ' A path in the composition and what it bound.
    : path=path binds=row[weave/bind]
  + placed
    : pos=weave/position binds=row[weave/bind]
  + ask
    ' One ask this world is to answer: where the arguments stand, the
    ' thing they are asked of, the action, and the world that asked.
    : place=path thing=path action=str asker=nat
  + place
    ' One place of a composition as the world acting sees it: where it is
    ' in the composition (spot); how it stands (kind: held, todo, may,
    ' waits, unproven or unfit); the world that writes there (by); and where this world holds
    ' the record, or would write it (held).
    : spot=path kind=str by=nat held=path
  + stood
    ' A record of a composition that checked: where it stands, the record,
    ' the world that said it (by) and the world it was written for (reader).
    : place=path record=myth by=nat reader=nat
  + pattern
    ' A path with captures, from how a table's row spells it:
    ' assignments/[a]/work/[s]. Nothing, for the top. None when a part is
    ' not a name.
    \ text=str
    ^ maybe[row[weave/seg]]
    = none=maybe[row[weave/seg]] .none
      empty=row[weave/seg] []
      parts (str/split_byte 47 text)
    ? (eq 0 text.len) (./some empty)
    % i=nat 0
      out=row[weave/seg] empty
    ^ maybe[row[weave/seg]]
    ? (ge i parts.len) (./some out)
    = part parts.at(i)
      held (and (gt part.len 2) (and (eq 91 part.at(0)) (eq 93 part.at(part.len.dec))))
      word (? held (str/slice 1 (sub part.len 2) part) part)
    ?> (./some valid) (str/sym word) none
    = name=iota ($ts word)
    | _ i.inc out.snoc((weave/seg !held name))
  + whose
    ' Who a row names: the maker, when it says nothing or "maker"; else
    ' whoever fills the seats at the path it spells.
    \ text=str
    ^ maybe[weave/who]
    = none=maybe[weave/who] .none
      top=row[weave/seg] []
    ? (eq 0 text.len) (./some (weave/who .true top))
    ? (equal[str] text "maker") (./some (weave/who .true top))
    ?> (./some seats) (weave/pattern text) none
    | ./some (weave/who .false seats)
  + row
    ' One row of a table, from the record that states it: path, by, and
    ' for (several, with spaces between). None when it does not read.
    \ record=myth
    ^ maybe[weave/position]
    = none=maybe[weave/position] .none
    ?> (./some path) (weave/pattern record.txt_at(['path])) none
    | weave/rowed path record
  + shaped
    ' A position's path, from the shape a Grove norm publishes: its literal
    ' names fixed, its captures open under their own names.
    \ record=myth
    ^ maybe[row[weave/seg]]
    = none=maybe[row[weave/seg]] .none
      empty=row[weave/seg] []
    ?> (./some held) record.get(system_vocabulary/grove/norm) none
    ?> schema=grove_norm_schema held none
    = segs
        | schema.segments.fold empty
          \ out=row[weave/seg] g=grove_norm_segment
          ^ row[weave/seg]
          ? g.pattern
           > (zeta/lit value) out.snoc((weave/seg .true value))
           > (zeta/var aura) out.snoc((weave/seg .false ($ts g.name)))
    | ./some segs
  + normed
    ' One row of a table, from a stencil a Grove unit publishes. Where it
    ' sits is the stencil's own pattern. Who writes and who reads are what
    ' its record says in by and for, spelled as a row spells them. The row
    ' names the stencil, and an action it names in apply, by where each
    ' sits in a world that holds the unit.
    \ source=path name=iota record=myth
    ^ maybe[weave/position]
    = none=maybe[weave/position] .none
      word record.txt_at(['apply])
      home=path (net/within source)
    ?> (./some path) (weave/shaped record) none
    ?> (./some row) (weave/rowed path record) none
    = p row.set_stencil((path_show home.snoc(name)))
    ? (eq 0 word.len) (./some p)
    ?> (./some valid) (str/sym word) none
    = action=iota ($ts word)
    | ./some p.set_apply((path_show home.snoc(action)))
  + unit
    ' The table a Grove unit publishes: one row for each of its norms.
    \ root=path state=namespace
    ^ row[weave/position]
    = none=row[weave/position] []
    | (sovereign_peek root state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? !(eq rel.len 1) acc
      ?> (./some found) (weave/normed root rel.at(0) record) acc
      | acc.snoc(found)
  + spelled
    ' A path with captures, as a row spells it.
    \ segs=row[weave/seg]
    ^ str
    = parts
        | segs.map
          \ g=weave/seg
          ^ str
          = one=path [g.name]
            shown (path_show one)
            name (str/slice 1 (dec shown.len) shown)
          ? g.fixed name
          | str/cat_all ["[" name "]"]
    | str/join "/" parts
  + said
    ' Who a row names, as a row spells it.
    \ w=weave/who
    ^ str
    ? w.maker "maker"
    | weave/spelled w.seats
  + stated
    ' One row as the record that states it.
    \ p=weave/position
    ^ myth
    = readers (str/join " " p.readers.map((\ w=weave/who (weave/said w))))
      base=myth
        . (myth/sing ['path] (pails/t (weave/spelled p.path)))
          put(['by] (pails/t (weave/said p.writer)))
          put(['for] (pails/t readers))
      applied=myth (? (eq 0 p.apply.len) base base.put(['apply] (pails/t p.apply)))
      shown=myth (? (eq 0 p.shows.len) applied applied.put(['shows] (pails/t p.shows)))
    ? (eq 0 p.stencil.len) shown
    | shown.put(['stencil] (pails/t p.stencil))
  + own
    ' The table's own row: the maker writes the rows, and everyone who
    ' could sit anywhere reads them.
    \ table=row[weave/position]
    ^ weave/position
    = top=row[weave/seg] []
      nowhere=path []
      at=row[weave/seg] [(weave/seg .true 'table) (weave/seg .false 'n)]
      bare (weave/comp 0 nowhere table)
      readers
        | (weave/named bare).map
          \ seats=row[weave/seg]
          ^ weave/who
          | weave/who .false seats
    | weave/position at (weave/who .true top) readers "" "" ""
  + whole
    ' A table with the rows every composition has: the table's own; the
    ' top of the tree, which the maker writes for the same readers unless
    ' the table says otherwise; and beside each row that applies an
    ' action, its answer.
    \ table=row[weave/position]
    ^ row[weave/position]
    = own (weave/own table)
      top=row[weave/seg] []
      first=row[weave/position] [own]
      apex=row[weave/position] [(weave/position top own.writer own.readers "" "" "")]
      said (table.any((\ p=weave/position (eq 0 p.path.len))))
      body (? said table apex.weld(table))
    | first.weld(body).weld((weave/answered body))
  + answered
    ' The row beside each row that applies an action: the answer, which
    ' whoever writes the thing writes for whoever asked. A table that
    ' states that row itself is left as it says.
    \ table=row[weave/position]
    ^ row[weave/position]
    = none=row[weave/position] []
      nowhere=path []
      bare (weave/comp 0 nowhere table)
    | table.fold none
      \ acc=row[weave/position] p=weave/position
      ^ row[weave/position]
      ? (eq 0 p.apply.len) acc
      ?> (./some thing) (weave/parent bare p) acc
      = beside=row[weave/seg] p.path.snoc((weave/seg .true 'answer))
        shown (weave/spelled beside)
        asker=row[weave/who] [p.writer]
      ? (table.any((\ q=weave/position (equal[str] shown (weave/spelled q.path))))) acc
      | acc.snoc((weave/position beside thing.writer asker "" "" ""))
  + tabled
    ' A table as records beneath a composition's own tree, where its maker
    ' writes them for everyone: the table's own row first, then the top,
    ' then each row, written where it differs from what is there.
    \ table=row[weave/position] root=path state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      rows (weave/whole table)
    % i=nat 0
      out=row[[p=path q=writ]] none
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    ? (ge i rows.len) out
    = target=path root.weld(['table ($u i.inc)])
      record (weave/stated rows.at(i))
    ? (equal[myth] record (sovereign_care .x target state).fil.fall(myth/new)) (_ i.inc out)
    | _ i.inc out.snoc([target (writ/make record)])
  + rowed
    ' The rest of a row, once its path is known: who writes, who reads.
    \ path=row[weave/seg] record=myth
    ^ maybe[weave/position]
    = none=maybe[weave/position] .none
      nobody=row[weave/who] []
    ?> (./some writer) (weave/whose record.txt_at(['by])) none
    = readers
        | (str/split_byte 32 record.txt_at(['for])).fold nobody
          \ out=row[weave/who] part=str
          ^ row[weave/who]
          ? (eq 0 part.len) out
          ?> (./some reader) (weave/whose part) out
          | out.snoc(reader)
    | ./some (weave/position path writer readers record.txt_at(['apply]) record.txt_at(['shows]) record.txt_at(['stencil]))
  + rows
    ' The table of a composition, as this world holds it from the maker:
    ' the records beneath table, in the order of their names.
    \ maker=nat rel=path s=weave/side state=namespace
    ^ row[weave/position]
    = none=row[weave/position] []
      bare (weave/comp maker rel none)
      kept=path (weave/from bare s maker).snoc('table)
    | (sovereign_peek kept state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [at record]
      ? !(eq at.len 1) acc
      ?> (./some found) (weave/row record) acc
      | acc.snoc(found)
  + same
    ' Whether two path segments are the same, whatever kind each is.
    \ a=iota b=iota
    ^ bool
    = one=path [a]
      two=path [b]
    | equal[str] (path_show one) (path_show two)
  + match
    ' What a path binds against a pattern; none when it is not at it.
    \ pattern=row[weave/seg] where=path
    ^ maybe[row[weave/bind]]
    = none=maybe[row[weave/bind]] .none
      empty=row[weave/bind] []
    ? !(eq pattern.len where.len) none
    % i=nat 0
      out=row[weave/bind] empty
    ^ maybe[row[weave/bind]]
    ? (ge i pattern.len) (./some out)
    = s pattern.at(i)
    ? (and s.fixed !(weave/same s.name where.at(i))) none
    ? s.fixed (_ i.inc out)
    | _ i.inc out.snoc((weave/bind s.name where.at(i)))
  + bound
    ' What a capture is bound to; none when it is not.
    \ name=iota binds=row[weave/bind]
    ^ maybe[iota]
    = none=maybe[iota] .none
    | binds.fold none
      \ acc=maybe[iota] b=weave/bind
      ^ maybe[iota]
      ? (maybe/is_some acc) acc
      ? !(weave/same b.name name) acc
      | ./some b.value
  + agrees
    ' Whether what a path bound is what was already bound.
    \ got=row[weave/bind] binds=row[weave/bind]
    ^ bool
    % i=nat 0
    ^ bool
    ? (ge i got.len) .true
    = g got.at(i)
    ?> (./some value) (weave/bound g.name binds) (_ i.inc)
    ? !(weave/same value g.value) .false
    | _ i.inc
  + from
    ' Where this world holds what a world wrote of the composition: its
    ' own side, or beneath that world's root for it, under the
    ' composition's own name.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side writer=nat
    ^ path
    = theirs=path [($x s.me) 'her ($x writer) ($x c.maker)]
    ? (eq writer s.me) s.root
    | theirs.weld(c.rel)
  + to
    ' Where this world writes a copy for a reader.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side reader=nat
    ^ path
    = base=path [($x s.me) 'our ($x reader) ($x c.maker)]
    | base.weld(c.rel)
  + seen
    ' The record at a path, as this world holds it from the world that
    ' writes there. From nobody else.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side writer=nat where=path state=namespace
    ^ maybe[myth]
    = none=maybe[myth] .none
    ? (eq 0 writer) none
    = here=path (weave/from c s writer).weld(where)
      until (weave/left c s writer where state)
    ? (eq 0 until) (sovereign_care .x here state).fil
    ?> (./known record) (state.local.x_at(until here)) none
    | ./some record
  + seat
    ' The one seat a who names for what a path bound, where this world
    ' holds it from the maker. None for the maker, or where a capture is
    ' left open and so names every seat.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side w=weave/who binds=row[weave/bind]
    ^ maybe[path]
    = none=maybe[path] .none
    ? w.maker none
    ?> (./some rel) (weave/filled w.seats binds) none
    | ./some (weave/from c s c.maker).weld(rel)
  + sat_in
    ' Every world that has filled a seat, newest first, read off the
    ' seat's own cases as this world holds them. A seat is read at a case:
    ' who filled it when a record was written is who wrote the record,
    ' whoever fills it now.
    \ seat=path state=namespace
    ^ row[weave/tenure]
    = none=row[weave/tenure] []
    % k=nat state.case(.x seat).fall(0)
      later=nat 0
      out=row[weave/tenure] none
    ^ row[weave/tenure]
    ? (eq 0 k) out
    ?> (./some epoch) (namespace/epoch .x (./some k) seat state.local) out
    = world=nat
        ?> (./known record) (state.local.x_at(epoch seat)) 0
        | record.nat_at(['world] 0)
      last=nat (? (eq 0 out.len) 0 out.at(out.len.dec).world)
      fresh (and (gt world 0) !(and (gt out.len 0) (eq last world)))
      next (? fresh out.snoc((weave/tenure world later)) out)
    | _ k.dec epoch next
  + left
    ' This world's own epoch at which it held that a world no longer
    ' filled the seat that writes a place: 0 while it fills it, and for
    ' the maker and this world itself. What that world wrote there is read
    ' as this world held it then, so nothing it says afterwards is taken.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side writer=nat where=path state=namespace
    ^ nat
    ? (eq writer s.me) 0
    ?> (./some found) (weave/find c where) 0
    ?> (./some seat) (weave/seat c s found.pos.writer found.binds) 0
    = line (weave/sat_in seat state).keep((\ one=weave/tenure (eq one.world writer)))
    ? (eq 0 line.len) 0
    | line.at(0).until
  + sitters
    ' The worlds that fill the seats a path names, with what is bound put
    ' in: one seat when every capture is bound, every seat there when one
    ' is left open. A seat nobody fills names nobody.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side seats=row[weave/seg] binds=row[weave/bind] state=namespace
    ^ row[nat]
    = none=row[nat] []
    | (sovereign_peek (weave/from c s c.maker) state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ?> (./some got) (weave/match seats rel) acc
      ? !(weave/agrees got binds) acc
      = w record.nat_at(['world] 0)
      ? (eq 0 w) acc
      ? (acc.any((\ had=nat (eq had w)))) acc
      | acc.snoc(w)
  + worlds
    ' The worlds a who names, for a position whose path bound these.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side w=weave/who binds=row[weave/bind] state=namespace
    ^ row[nat]
    = maker=row[nat] [c.maker]
    ? w.maker maker
    | weave/sitters c s w.seats binds state
  + find
    ' The table's position a path is at, with what it binds.
    \ c=weave/comp where=path
    ^ maybe[weave/placed]
    = none=maybe[weave/placed] .none
    | c.table.fold none
      \ acc=maybe[weave/placed] p=weave/position
      ^ maybe[weave/placed]
      ? (maybe/is_some acc) acc
      ?> (./some binds) (weave/match p.path where) acc
      | ./some (weave/placed p binds)
  + writes
    ' Whether this world is one that writes at a placed path.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side found=weave/placed state=namespace
    ^ bool
    | (weave/worlds c s found.pos.writer found.binds state).any((\ w=nat (eq w s.me)))
  + reads
    ' Whether this world is a reader of a placed path.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side found=weave/placed state=namespace
    ^ bool
    % i=nat 0
    ^ bool
    ? (ge i found.pos.readers.len) .false
    ? ((weave/worlds c s found.pos.readers.at(i) found.binds state).any((\ w=nat (eq w s.me)))) .true
    | _ i.inc
  + audience
    ' Every reader of a placed path but this world, once each.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side found=weave/placed state=namespace
    ^ row[nat]
    = none=row[nat] []
    | found.pos.readers.fold none
      \ acc=row[nat] w=weave/who
      ^ row[nat]
      | (weave/worlds c s w found.binds state).fold acc
        \ had=row[nat] reader=nat
        ^ row[nat]
        ? (eq reader s.me) had
        ? (had.any((\ old=nat (eq old reader)))) had
        | had.snoc(reader)
  + named
    ' Every seat path the table names: wherever a row says who writes or
    ' who reads, other than the maker. A position is a seat because some
    ' row names it, and for no other reason.
    \ c=weave/comp
    ^ row[row[weave/seg]]
    = none=row[row[weave/seg]] []
    | c.table.fold none
      \ acc=row[row[weave/seg]] p=weave/position
      ^ row[row[weave/seg]]
      = first (? p.writer.maker acc (weave/once p.writer.seats acc))
      | p.readers.fold first
        \ out=row[row[weave/seg]] w=weave/who
        ^ row[row[weave/seg]]
        ? w.maker out
        | weave/once w.seats out
  + once
    ' A seat path added to those named, unless it is there under the same
    ' spelling.
    \ seats=row[weave/seg] had=row[row[weave/seg]]
    ^ row[row[weave/seg]]
    = shown (weave/spelled seats)
    ? (had.any((\ old=row[weave/seg] (equal[str] shown (weave/spelled old))))) had
    | had.snoc(seats)
  + everyone
    ' The maker and every world that fills a seat.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side state=namespace
    ^ row[nat]
    = start=row[nat] [c.maker]
      open=row[weave/bind] []
    | (weave/named c).fold start
      \ acc=row[nat] seats=row[weave/seg]
      ^ row[nat]
      | (weave/sitters c s seats open state).fold acc
        \ had=row[nat] w=nat
        ^ row[nat]
        ? (had.any((\ old=nat (eq old w)))) had
        | had.snoc(w)
  + copies
    ' One record of this world's own, named for each of its readers: what
    ' is written in a reader's root is a reference to the record at its
    ' case, which publication enters as that record (net/standin). So the
    ' record is never made a second time. Written only where the reference
    ' there differs.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side rel=path readers=row[nat] acc=row[[p=path q=writ]] state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = source=path s.root.weld(rel)
    ?> (./some case) state.case(.x source) acc
    = stand (myth/sing ['is] (safe case .x source))
    | readers.fold acc
      \ out=row[[p=path q=writ]] reader=nat
      ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
      = target=path (weave/to c s reader).weld(rel)
      ? (equal[myth] stand (sovereign_care .x target state).fil.fall(myth/new)) out
      | out.snoc([target (writ/make stand)])
  + roots
    ' A root in this world for every other world in the composition, made
    ' where there is none, so that what is written for it has somewhere to
    ' be published from.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
    | (weave/everyone c s state).fold none
      \ out=row[[p=path q=writ]] w=nat
      ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
      = base=path [($x s.me) 'our ($x w)]
      ? (eq w s.me) out
      ? (net/live base state) out
      | out.snoc([base (writ/make myth/new)])
  + tell
    ' What this world must write into other worlds' roots: each record of
    ' its own that sits where it writes, named for every reader of that
    ' position (weave/copies), and only where that differs. A record of its
    ' own that sits where it does not write is passed over: it is nobody's
    ' to read.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = head (weave/roots c s state)
    | (sovereign_peek s.root state).tap.fold head
      \ acc [rel record]
      ?> (./some found) (weave/find c rel) acc
      ? !(weave/writes c s found state) acc
      | weave/copies c s rel (weave/audience c s found state) acc state
  + begins
    ' Whether one pattern is the start of another.
    \ short=row[weave/seg] long=row[weave/seg]
    ^ bool
    ? (ge short.len long.len) .false
    % i=nat 0
    ^ bool
    ? (ge i short.len) .true
    = a short.at(i)
      b long.at(i)
      alike (? a.fixed b.fixed !(b.fixed))
    ? !alike .false
    ? !(weave/same a.name b.name) .false
    | _ i.inc
  + parent
    ' The position a position sits beneath: the longest one whose path
    ' its own begins with.
    \ c=weave/comp p=weave/position
    ^ maybe[weave/position]
    = none=maybe[weave/position] .none
    | c.table.fold none
      \ acc=maybe[weave/position] q=weave/position
      ^ maybe[weave/position]
      ? !(weave/begins q.path p.path) acc
      ?> (./some best) acc (./some q)
      ? (gt q.path.len best.path.len) (./some q)
      acc
  + names
    ' Whether a pattern has a capture of this name.
    \ name=iota pattern=row[weave/seg]
    ^ bool
    | pattern.any((\ g=weave/seg (and !(g.fixed) (weave/same g.name name))))
  + seated
    ' Every seat a path names that a world has ever filled, as what each
    ' binds beyond what is bound.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side seats=row[weave/seg] binds=row[weave/bind] state=namespace
    ^ row[row[weave/bind]]
    = none=row[row[weave/bind]] []
    | (sovereign_peek (weave/from c s c.maker) state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ?> (./some got) (weave/match seats rel) acc
      ? !(weave/agrees got binds) acc
      ? (eq 0 (weave/sat_in (weave/from c s c.maker).weld(rel) state).len) acc
      | acc.snoc(got)
  + grow
    ' One spot taken one segment further, for a position. A fixed name is
    ' added. A capture the spot already binds is put in. A capture the
    ' position's writer is told by ranges over the seats there. Any other
    ' capture ranges over what its writer has put there: such a position
    ' is one its writer adds to, and has no empty places of its own.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side p=weave/position g=weave/seg at=weave/spot state=namespace
    ^ row[weave/spot]
    = plain=row[weave/spot] [(weave/spot at.path.snoc(g.name) at.binds)]
    ? g.fixed plain
    ?> (./some value) (weave/bound g.name at.binds) (weave/range c s p g at state)
    = put=row[weave/spot] [(weave/spot at.path.snoc(value) at.binds)]
    put
  + range
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side p=weave/position g=weave/seg at=weave/spot state=namespace
    ^ row[weave/spot]
    = none=row[weave/spot] []
      told (and !(p.writer.maker) (weave/names g.name p.writer.seats))
    ? told
      | (weave/seated c s p.writer.seats at.binds state).fold none
        \ out=row[weave/spot] got=row[weave/bind]
        ^ row[weave/spot]
        ?> (./some value) (weave/bound g.name got) out
        | out.snoc((weave/spot at.path.snoc(value) at.binds.snoc((weave/bind g.name value))))
    = by (weave/worlds c s p.writer at.binds state)
    ? !(eq 1 by.len) none
    | (sovereign_peek (weave/from c s by.at(0)).weld(at.path) state).kid_tap.fold none
      \ out=row[weave/spot] [key tree]
      ^ row[weave/spot]
      | out.snoc((weave/spot at.path.snoc(key) at.binds.snoc((weave/bind g.name key))))
  + spots
    ' Every spot a position could be at, beneath the places its parent
    ' stands at: the tail of its path grown segment by segment.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side p=weave/position state=namespace
    ^ row[weave/spot]
    = empty=path []
      free=row[weave/bind] []
      top=row[weave/spot] [(weave/spot empty free)]
      above=maybe[weave/position] (weave/parent c p)
      starts
        ?> (./some q) above top
        | weave/stands c s q state
      skip
        ?> (./some q) above 0
        | q.path.len
    % i=nat skip
      now=row[weave/spot] starts
    ^ row[weave/spot]
    ? (ge i p.path.len) now
    = g p.path.at(i)
      none=row[weave/spot] []
      next
        | now.fold none
          \ out=row[weave/spot] at=weave/spot
          ^ row[weave/spot]
          | out.weld((weave/grow c s p g at state))
    | _ i.inc next
  + writer_of
    ' The one world that writes at a spot of a position: whoever of those
    ' that have filled its seat last wrote there, and where none has, the
    ' world that fills the seat now. So a seat given to another world
    ' changes who writes next and never who wrote. 0 when nobody does yet,
    ' or it is not one.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side p=weave/position at=weave/spot state=namespace
    ^ nat
    = by (weave/worlds c s p.writer at.binds state)
      now (? (eq 1 by.len) by.at(0) 0)
    ?> (./some seat) (weave/seat c s p.writer at.binds) now
    = wrote (weave/sat_in seat state).keep((\ one=weave/tenure (maybe/is_some (weave/seen c s one.world at.path state))))
    ? (eq 0 wrote.len) now
    | wrote.at(0).world
  + fits
    ' Whether a record has the shape its row's stencil gives, judged by the
    ' contract of that stencil as this world itself holds it. So a record
    ' another world wrote is judged where it is read, and a landing is
    ' never refused for its shape. A row that names no stencil, and a
    ' stencil this world does not hold, judge nothing.
    \ p=weave/position record=myth state=namespace
    ^ bool
    ? (eq 0 p.stencil.len) .true
    ?> (./some rel) (path_parse p.stencil) .true
    = base=path [state.self]
    ?> (./some declared) (sovereign_care .x base.weld(rel) state).fil .true
    ?> (./some held) declared.get(system_vocabulary/grove/role_contract) .true
    ?> contract=lash held .true
    | maybe/is_none (fit_check record.put(system_vocabulary/lash contract))
  + fields
    ' The slots a record at a row may hold, by name, as the row's stencil
    ' declares them and this world holds it. A name ends in ? where the
    ' slot may be left out. Nothing, for a row that names no stencil or
    ' one this world does not hold.
    \ p=weave/position state=namespace
    ^ row[str]
    = none=row[str] []
    ?> (./some rel) (path_parse p.stencil) none
    = base=path [state.self]
    ?> (./some declared) (sovereign_care .x base.weld(rel) state).fil none
    ?> (./some held) declared.get(system_vocabulary/grove/norm) none
    ?> schema=grove_norm_schema held none
    | schema.item.fields.fold none
      \ out=row[str] f=grove_role_field
      ^ row[str]
      | out.snoc((? f.optional (str/cat_all [f.name "?"]) f.name))
  + stands
    ' Where a position has a record, as this world holds it from whoever
    ' writes each. A record stands only when it has the shape its row
    ' gives (weave/fits) and, at a place that must show something, shows
    ' it (weave/proved).
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side p=weave/position state=namespace
    ^ row[weave/spot]
    = none=row[weave/spot] []
    | (weave/spots c s p state).fold none
      \ out=row[weave/spot] at=weave/spot
      ^ row[weave/spot]
      ?> (./some record) (weave/seen c s (weave/writer_of c s p at state) at.path state) out
      ? !(weave/fits p record state) out
      ? (and (gt p.shows.len 0) !(either/is_ok (weave/proved c s p at state))) out
      | out.snoc(at)
  + writable
    ' Whether a place is this world's to write now: a row of the table
    ' puts it, this world is the one that writes there, and the place it
    ' sits beneath stands. So a new member of a collection its writer adds
    ' to is writable, and nothing beneath an empty place is.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side where=path state=namespace
    ^ bool
    ?> (./some found) (weave/find c where) .false
    ? (weave/describes found.pos) .false
    ? !(weave/writes c s found state) .false
    ?> (./some above) (weave/parent c found.pos) .true
    = under=path where.take(above.path.len)
      held (weave/stands c s above state).keep((\ at=weave/spot (equal[path] at.path under)))
    | gt held.len 0
  + todo
    ' What this world has to do next: every place it writes, beneath
    ' places that stand, that is empty. A place where it may ask for an
    ' action is not something it has to do, and is left to may.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side state=namespace
    ^ row[path]
    | weave/empty .false c s state
  + may
    ' What this world may ask: every empty place it writes, beneath places
    ' that stand, at a position that applies an action.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side state=namespace
    ^ row[path]
    | weave/empty .true c s state
  + empty
    ' The empty places this world writes: those that ask for an action, or
    ' the others.
    \ asking=bool c=weave/comp s=weave/side state=namespace
    ^ row[path]
    = none=row[path] []
    | c.table.fold none
      \ acc=row[path] p=weave/position
      ^ row[path]
      ? (? asking (eq 0 p.apply.len) (gt p.apply.len 0)) acc
      | (weave/spots c s p state).fold acc
        \ out=row[path] at=weave/spot
        ^ row[path]
        ? !(eq s.me (weave/writer_of c s p at state)) out
        ? (maybe/is_some (weave/seen c s s.me at.path state)) out
        | out.snoc(at.path)
  + waits
    ' What this world waits on: every place it reads, beneath places that
    ' stand, that its writer has left empty; with who that writer is.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side state=namespace
    ^ row[[place=path on=nat]]
    = none=row[[place=path on=nat]] []
    | c.table.fold none
      \ acc=row[[place=path on=nat]] p=weave/position
      ^ row[[place=path on=nat]]
      | (weave/spots c s p state).fold acc
        \ out=row[[place=path on=nat]] at=weave/spot
        ^ row[[place=path on=nat]]
        = by (weave/writer_of c s p at state)
        ? (eq by s.me) out
        ? (eq 0 by) out
        ? !(weave/reads c s (weave/placed p at.binds) state) out
        ? (maybe/is_some (weave/seen c s by at.path state)) out
        | out.snoc([at.path by])
  + asked
    ' The asks this world is to answer: at each position that applies an
    ' action, each place where the asker's record stands, beneath a thing
    ' this world writes, that this world has not answered. An ask is read
    ' only from the world that writes its position, as anything is.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side state=namespace
    ^ row[weave/ask]
    = none=row[weave/ask] []
    | c.table.fold none
      \ acc=row[weave/ask] p=weave/position
      ^ row[weave/ask]
      ? (eq 0 p.apply.len) acc
      ?> (./some q) (weave/parent c p) acc
      | (weave/stands c s p state).fold acc
        \ out=row[weave/ask] at=weave/spot
        ^ row[weave/ask]
        = thing=path at.path.take(q.path.len)
          reply=path at.path.snoc('answer)
          by (weave/worlds c s q.writer at.binds state)
        ? !(eq 1 by.len) out
        ? !(eq s.me by.at(0)) out
        ? (maybe/is_some (weave/seen c s s.me reply state)) out
        | out.snoc((weave/ask at.path thing p.apply (weave/writer_of c s p at state)))
  + applied
    ' One ask applied: the thing as it would then be, or why not. The
    ' handler is the one this world itself holds at the action's path.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side a=weave/ask target=path state=namespace
    ^ either[str myth]
    ?> (./some arguments) (weave/seen c s a.asker a.place state) (./err "the ask is not held")
    ?> (./some current) (sovereign_care .x target state).fil (./err "nothing stands there")
    ?> (./some rel) (path_parse a.action) (./err "the action is not named")
    = base=path [state.self]
      held=path base.weld(rel)
    ?> (./some declaration) (sovereign_care .x held state).fil (./err "this world does not hold the action")
    ?> (./some code) declaration.get(system_vocabulary/grove/action_handler) (./err "this world does not hold the action")
    ?> handler=grove_action_handler code (./err "this world does not hold the action")
    = invoke handler.apply
    ?> (./ok result) (Try (invoke arguments) current) (./err "the action failed")
    ?> (./some next) result (./err "the action refused")
    | ./ok next
  + no
    ' An answer that says not, and why.
    \ why=str
    ^ myth
    | (myth/sing ['done] (pails/n 2)).put(['why] (pails/t why))
  + answers
    ' The asks this world is to answer, answered. Where the action
    ' applies, the thing is written anew and the answer beside the ask
    ' says done (1). Where the handler refuses or fails, or this world
    ' does not hold it, or nothing stands at the thing, the answer says
    ' not (2), and why. One ask of a thing is answered at a time, so a
    ' second is applied to the thing as the first left it.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
    | (weave/asked c s state).fold none
      \ out=row[[p=path q=writ]] a=weave/ask
      ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
      = asked=path s.root.weld(a.place)
        reply=path asked.snoc('answer)
        target=path s.root.weld(a.thing)
      ? (out.any((\ [where change] (equal[path] where target)))) out
      ? (weave/applied c s a target state)
       > (./err why)
        = refusal=[p=path q=writ] [reply (writ/make (weave/no why))]
        | out.snoc(refusal)
       > (./ok next)
        = changed=[p=path q=writ] [target (writ/make next)]
          done=[p=path q=writ] [reply (writ/make (myth/sing ['done] (pails/n 1)))]
        | out.snoc(changed).snoc(done)
  + laid
    ' The composition as the world acting sees it: one tree, laid over its
    ' sides. Every place this world writes or reads, beneath places that
    ' stand, with how it stands. held: a record is there, from whoever
    ' writes there. todo: empty, and this world's to write. may: empty,
    ' and this world may ask there. waits: empty, and another's to write.
    ' unproven: a record is there that must show something, and does not.
    ' unfit: a record is there that has not the shape its row gives.
    ' The table's own rows are how the composition is described and are
    ' not places in it. Nothing here writes: it is a reading, and Goo, a
    ' door and an agent read the same one.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side state=namespace
    ^ row[weave/place]
    = none=row[weave/place] []
    | c.table.fold none
      \ acc=row[weave/place] p=weave/position
      ^ row[weave/place]
      ? (weave/describes p) acc
      | (weave/spots c s p state).fold acc
        \ out=row[weave/place] at=weave/spot
        ^ row[weave/place]
        = by (weave/writer_of c s p at state)
          mine (eq by s.me)
          root=path (weave/from c s by)
          where=path root.weld(at.path)
          found (weave/seen c s by at.path state)
          there (maybe/is_some found)
          fit (weave/fits p found.fall(myth/new) state)
          open=str (? mine (? (gt p.apply.len 0) "may" "todo") "waits")
          shown ((eq 0 p.shows.len) || (either/is_ok (weave/proved c s p at state)))
          full=str (? fit (? shown "held" "unproven") "unfit")
          kind=str (? there full open)
        ? (eq 0 by) out
        ? (and !mine !(weave/reads c s (weave/placed p at.binds) state)) out
        | out.snoc((weave/place at.path kind by where))
  + describes
    ' Whether a position is one of the table's own rows.
    \ p=weave/position
    ^ bool
    ? (eq 0 p.path.len) .false
    = first p.path.at(0)
    | and first.fixed (weave/same first.name 'table)
  + world
    ' A world's name as a path spells it.
    \ w=nat
    ^ str
    = one=path [($x w)]
      shown (path_show one)
    | str/slice 1 (dec shown.len) shown
  + shown
    ' A laid composition as lines of text, one a place: how it stands,
    ' the place, where this world holds it or would write it, and the
    ' world that writes there.
    \ places=row[weave/place]
    ^ str
    = lines
        | places.map
          \ item=weave/place
          ^ str
          | str/cat_all [item.kind " " (path_show item.spot) " " (path_show item.held) " " (weave/world item.by)]
    | str/join (str/from_atom 10) lines
  + within
    ' Where a publisher's name stands in a composition, and whom it was
    ' written for: /<publisher>/our/<reader>/<maker>/<rel>/<place>. None
    ' when the name is not within this composition.
    \ maker=nat rel=path name=path
    ^ maybe[[reader=nat place=path]]
    = none=maybe[[reader=nat place=path]] .none
      head (add 4 rel.len)
    ? (lt name.len head) none
    ? !(weave/same name.at(1) 'our) none
    ? !(weave/same name.at(3) ($x maker)) none
    ? !(equal[path] rel name.take(head).drop(4)) none
    = got=[reader=nat place=path] [(quip_val name.at(2)) name.drop(head)]
    | ./some got
  + facts
    ' Every witness of a proof that checks and is within a composition, as
    ' what it says: the place, the record, who said it and for whom.
    \ maker=nat rel=path proof=row[pass/witness]
    ^ row[weave/stood]
    = none=row[weave/stood] []
    | proof.fold none
      \ out=row[weave/stood] w=pass/witness
      ^ row[weave/stood]
      = by (pass/speaker w)
      ? (eq 0 by) out
      ?> (./some got) (weave/within maker rel w.name) out
      = [reader place] got
      | out.snoc((weave/stood place w.record by reader))
  + told
    ' What the maker said at a place, in a proof.
    \ maker=nat said=row[weave/stood] place=path
    ^ maybe[myth]
    = none=maybe[myth] .none
    | said.fold none
      \ acc=maybe[myth] f=weave/stood
      ^ maybe[myth]
      ? (maybe/is_some acc) acc
      ? !(eq f.by maker) acc
      ? !(equal[path] f.place place) acc
      | ./some f.record
  + ruled
    ' The table's position a place is at, as a proof carries the table.
    ' The maker's rows are read in order from the first, as the
    ' composition itself reads them, so a proof that leaves out a row
    ' before the one it wants says nothing.
    \ maker=nat said=row[weave/stood] place=path
    ^ maybe[weave/placed]
    = none=maybe[weave/placed] .none
    % k=nat 1
    ^ maybe[weave/placed]
    = at=path ['table ($u k)]
    ?> (./some record) (weave/told maker said at) none
    ?> (./some p) (weave/row record) (_ k.inc)
    ?> (./some binds) (weave/match p.path place) (_ k.inc)
    | ./some (weave/placed p binds)
  + sat
    ' Whether the maker said, in a proof, that a world fills a seat a path
    ' names, with these bound.
    \ maker=nat said=row[weave/stood] seats=row[weave/seg] binds=row[weave/bind] w=nat
    ^ bool
    | said.any
      \ f=weave/stood
      ^ bool
      ? !(eq f.by maker) .false
      ?> (./some got) (weave/match seats f.place) .false
      ? !(weave/agrees got binds) .false
      | eq w f.record.nat_at(['world] 0)
  + vouched
    ' What a proof shows of a composition, to a world that holds nothing
    ' of it but its maker's name and where its tree sits there. A record
    ' is shown when its publisher said it, at a place of the composition;
    ' the maker's table, as the proof carries it, puts that place at a
    ' position; and the maker writes there itself, or said, in a seat the
    ' proof carries, that the publisher fills the seat that does. Nobody
    ' is asked. What is shown is what was said, at the versions shown: a
    ' proof does not say the maker says so still.
    \ maker=nat rel=path proof=row[pass/witness]
    ^ row[weave/stood]
    = none=row[weave/stood] []
      said (weave/facts maker rel proof)
    | said.fold none
      \ out=row[weave/stood] f=weave/stood
      ^ row[weave/stood]
      ?> (./some found) (weave/ruled maker said f.place) out
      ? (weave/describes found.pos) out
      ? found.pos.writer.maker
        ? (eq f.by maker) out.snoc(f)
        out
      ? !(weave/sat maker said found.pos.writer.seats found.binds f.by) out
      | out.snoc(f)
  + ruling
    ' The maker's table as this world holds it, as witnesses: each row
    ' from the first to the one that puts a place. None when a row is
    ' missing or cannot be shown.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side place=path state=namespace
    ^ maybe[row[pass/witness]]
    = none=maybe[row[pass/witness]] .none
      empty=row[pass/witness] []
      base=path (weave/from c s c.maker)
    % k=nat 1
      out=row[pass/witness] empty
    ^ maybe[row[pass/witness]]
    = tail=path ['table ($u k)]
      at=path base.weld(tail)
    ?> (./some record) (sovereign_care .x at state).fil none
    ?> (./some w) (pass/witnessed s.me c.maker at state) none
    = next out.snoc(w)
    ?> (./some p) (weave/row record) (_ k.inc next)
    ?> (./some binds) (weave/match p.path place) (_ k.inc next)
    | ./some next
  + seat_of
    ' The seat, among those a path names with these bound, that the maker
    ' says a world fills.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side seats=row[weave/seg] binds=row[weave/bind] w=nat state=namespace
    ^ maybe[path]
    = none=maybe[path] .none
    | (sovereign_peek (weave/from c s c.maker) state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? (maybe/is_some acc) acc
      ?> (./some got) (weave/match seats rel) acc
      ? !(weave/agrees got binds) acc
      ? !(eq w record.nat_at(['world] 0)) acc
      | ./some rel
  + carry
    ' What this world holds of a place in a composition, as a proof for a
    ' world that holds nothing of it: the maker's table as far as the row
    ' that puts the place, the record from the world that writes there,
    ' and the seat in which the maker says that world sits. Empty unless
    ' all of it is held as its publishers said it. A place this world
    ' writes itself is not something it was given, and is not carried.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side place=path state=namespace
    ^ row[pass/witness]
    = none=row[pass/witness] []
      nothing=maybe[[by=nat w=pass/witness]] .none
    ?> (./some found) (weave/find c place) none
    = thing
        | (weave/worlds c s found.pos.writer found.binds state).fold nothing
          \ acc=maybe[[by=nat w=pass/witness]] by=nat
          ^ maybe[[by=nat w=pass/witness]]
          ? (maybe/is_some acc) acc
          ? (eq by s.me) acc
          = at=path (weave/from c s by).weld(place)
          ?> (./some w) (pass/witnessed s.me by at state) acc
          = got=[by=nat w=pass/witness] [by w]
          | ./some got
    ?> (./some held) thing none
    ?> (./some rows) (weave/ruling c s place state) none
    = [by w] held
    = base rows.snoc(w)
    ? found.pos.writer.maker base
    ?> (./some seat) (weave/seat_of c s found.pos.writer.seats found.binds by state) none
    = at=path (weave/from c s c.maker).weld(seat)
    ?> (./some w) (pass/witnessed s.me c.maker at state) none
    | base.snoc(w)
  + want
    ' What a showing place wants shown: a record at a position of another
    ' composition. That composition is named by its maker and where its
    ' tree sits there; the position, by its path as that table spells it.
    : maker=nat rel=path at=row[weave/seg]
  + filled
    ' A pattern with what is bound put in: a path. None when a capture is
    ' not bound.
    \ pattern=row[weave/seg] binds=row[weave/bind]
    ^ maybe[path]
    = none=maybe[path] .none
      empty=path []
    % i=nat 0
      out=path empty
    ^ maybe[path]
    ? (ge i pattern.len) (./some out)
    = g pattern.at(i)
    ? g.fixed (_ i.inc out.snoc(g.name))
    ?> (./some value) (weave/bound g.name binds) none
    | _ i.inc out.snoc(value)
  + wanted
    ' What a showing position wants at a spot: read from the record at the
    ' place its row names, as this world holds it from whoever writes
    ' there. of is a reference to the composition where its maker keeps
    ' it, and at is the position's path.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side p=weave/position at=weave/spot state=namespace
    ^ maybe[weave/want]
    = none=maybe[weave/want] .none
    ? (eq 0 p.shows.len) none
    ?> (./some pattern) (weave/pattern p.shows) none
    ?> (./some where) (weave/filled pattern at.binds) none
    ?> (./some found) (weave/find c where) none
    = by (weave/worlds c s found.pos.writer found.binds state)
    ? !(eq 1 by.len) none
    ?> (./some record) (weave/seen c s by.at(0) where state) none
    ?> (./some held) record.get(['of]) none
    ?> link=safe held none
    ? (eq 0 link.path.len) none
    ?> (./some wants) (weave/pattern record.txt_at(['at])) none
    = maker (quip_val link.path.at(0))
    ? (eq 0 maker) none
    | ./some (weave/want maker (net/within link.path) wants)
  + proved
    ' What the record at a showing place shows: it carries a proof, as the
    ' bytes of its witnesses, so that it is the same in every world; the
    ' proof vouches a record of the composition wanted, at the position
    ' wanted; and that record was written for the world that shows it.
    ' What a world was given is its own to show, and nobody else's.
    ' Otherwise why not, as one word: the first of those that did not hold.
    ' No word, where no record is.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side p=weave/position at=weave/spot state=namespace
    ^ either[str weave/stood]
    = absent=str ""
      unasked=str "nothing-is-wanted-here"
      bare=str "it-carries-no-proof"
      unfit=str "its-proof-is-not-witnesses"
      unsigned=str "no-witness-checks-against-its-name"
      apart=str "no-witness-is-of-the-composition-wanted"
      unruled=str "the-table-or-the-seat-is-not-shown"
      other=str "written-for-another-world"
      elsewhere=str "not-at-the-position-wanted"
      by (weave/writer_of c s p at state)
    ?> (./some record) (weave/seen c s by at.path state) (./err absent)
    ?> (./some w) (weave/wanted c s p at state) (./err unasked)
    = bytes record.nat_at(['proof] 0)
    ? (eq 0 bytes) (./err bare)
    ?> (./some proof) (pass/unshown bytes) (./err unfit)
    = signed proof.keep((\ one=pass/witness !(eq 0 (pass/speaker one))))
      said (weave/facts w.maker w.rel proof)
      stood (weave/vouched w.maker w.rel proof)
      mine stood.keep((\ f=weave/stood (eq f.reader by)))
      right mine.keep((\ f=weave/stood (maybe/is_some (weave/match w.at f.place))))
    ? (eq 0 signed.len) (./err unsigned)
    ? (eq 0 said.len) (./err apart)
    ? (eq 0 stood.len) (./err unruled)
    ? (eq 0 mine.len) (./err other)
    ? (eq 0 right.len) (./err elsewhere)
    | ./ok right.at(0)
  + doubts
    ' A line for each record that does not stand, with why: it has not
    ' the shape its row gives (weave/fits), or it must show something and
    ' does not (weave/proved).
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side state=namespace
    ^ row[str]
    = none=row[str] []
      shape=str "not-the-shape-its-row-gives"
    | c.table.fold none
      \ acc=row[str] p=weave/position
      ^ row[str]
      ? (weave/describes p) acc
      | (weave/spots c s p state).fold acc
        \ out=row[str] at=weave/spot
        ^ row[str]
        ?> (./some record) (weave/seen c s (weave/writer_of c s p at state) at.path state) out
        ? !(weave/fits p record state) (out.snoc((str/cat_all ["why " (path_show at.path) " " shape])))
        ? (eq 0 p.shows.len) out
        ?> (./err why) (weave/proved c s p at state) out
        ? (eq 0 why.len) out
        | out.snoc((str/cat_all ["why " (path_show at.path) " " why]))
  + owes
    ' The showing places this world has chosen to fill and given no proof
    ' at: a record of its own stands there without one. With what each
    ' wants.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side state=namespace
    ^ row[[place=path want=weave/want]]
    = none=row[[place=path want=weave/want]] []
    | c.table.fold none
      \ acc=row[[place=path want=weave/want]] p=weave/position
      ^ row[[place=path want=weave/want]]
      ? (eq 0 p.shows.len) acc
      | (weave/spots c s p state).fold acc
        \ out=row[[place=path want=weave/want]] at=weave/spot
        ^ row[[place=path want=weave/want]]
        ? !(eq s.me (weave/writer_of c s p at state)) out
        ?> (./some record) (weave/seen c s s.me at.path state) out
        ? (maybe/is_some record.get(['proof])) out
        ?> (./some w) (weave/wanted c s p at state) out
        = item=[place=path want=weave/want] [at.path w]
        | out.snoc(item)
  + given
    ' The places of a composition, at a position's path, where this world
    ' holds a record another world wrote.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side at=row[weave/seg] state=namespace
    ^ row[path]
    = none=row[path] []
    | c.table.fold none
      \ acc=row[path] p=weave/position
      ^ row[path]
      ? (weave/describes p) acc
      | (weave/stands c s p state).fold acc
        \ out=row[path] spot=weave/spot
        ^ row[path]
        ? !(maybe/is_some (weave/match at spot.path)) out
        ? (eq s.me (weave/writer_of c s p spot state)) out
        | out.snoc(spot.path)
  + show
    ' The proof this world can give of what is wanted, from one
    ' composition it takes part in: what it holds at every place the want
    ' names. Empty when the want is of another composition, or nothing is
    ' held.
    \ c=weave/comp s=weave/side w=weave/want state=namespace
    ^ row[pass/witness]
    = none=row[pass/witness] []
    ? !(eq c.maker w.maker) none
    ? !(equal[path] c.rel w.rel) none
    | (weave/given c s w.at state).fold none
      \ out=row[pass/witness] place=path
      ^ row[pass/witness]
      | out.weld((weave/carry c s place state))
